{"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A drawing whose distances match the graph’s: stress majorization, the minimizer of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Kamada and Kawai’s energy that Graphviz’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"neato"},{"type":"text","text":" uses by default."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"stressMajorizationLayout","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"initial","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Drawing","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing\/Drawing","preciseIdentifier":"s:12GraphDrawing0B0V","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">? = nil, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"edgeLength","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": (","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Edges","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Edges-swift.associatedtype","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Index","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Double","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" = { _ in 1 }, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"tolerance","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Double","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" = 1e-4, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"maxIterations","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" = 1000) -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Drawing","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing\/Drawing","preciseIdentifier":"s:12GraphDrawing0B0V","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Discussion","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"discussion"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The target distance d_ij of two vertices is their shortest-path distance with "},{"code":"edgeLength","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(hops by default); between components it is 1 + L̄·√n, L̄ the mean edge length ("},{"code":"neato","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"‘s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"rule without packing). The drawing minimizes the stress Σ_{i<j} d_ij⁻² (‖x_i − x_j‖ − d_ij)²,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"which with these weights is Kamada and Kawai’s energy. Each step updates every vertex in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" order to the minimizer of a majorant of the stress in that vertex (Gansner,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Koren and North’s localized update), so the stress never increases. The run stops one step"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"after a step that lowered the stress by at most "},{"code":"tolerance","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" times its value (each step"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"measures its starting stress on the way), or after "},{"code":"maxIterations","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" steps. The default"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"tolerance, 10⁻⁴, is Graphviz’s "},{"code":"epsilon","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" for "},{"code":"neato -Gmode=major","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"; a smaller one can leave a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"plateau that 10⁻⁴ stops on (on a random 40-vertex graph, 10⁻⁵ ends 9% lower)."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The start is ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"initial"},{"text":", or by default ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"circularLayout(radius: L̄)"},{"text":": NetworkX’s start for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Kamada–Kawai, scaled by the mean edge length so that scaling every length by a power of 2","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"scales every step’s drawing by exactly that factor (the update is homogeneous), and any","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"other factor up to rounding. (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"neato -Gmode=major"},{"text":", the like-for-like Graphviz run, starts","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"from random positions.) Deterministic: no randomness anywhere. A directed graph is drawn","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"through ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"undirectedView"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Gansner, Koren and North, “Graph drawing by stress majorization”, Graph Drawing (GD"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"2004), LNCS 3383, 2005."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Kamada and Kawai, “An algorithm for drawing general undirected graphs”, Information"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Processing Letters 31(1), 1989."}]}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"O(n·(n + m)) for the distances by breadth-first search (O(n·m log n) by Dijkstra when the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"lengths differ), then O(n²) per step. The reciprocal target distances are kept in single","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"precision for the pairs i < j only: 2n² bytes (200 MB at 10⁴ vertices), so ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"stress"},{"text":" and the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"drawing are those of distances rounded to about 7 significant digits.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Every edge length is positive and finite; ","type":"text"},{"code":"tolerance ≥ 0","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":";","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"maxIterations ≥ 0","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"; every vertex of the graph is in ","type":"text"},{"code":"initial","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", at a finite position,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"when it is given.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"style":"note","type":"aside","name":"Precondition"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/stressMajorizationLayout(initial:edgeLength:tolerance:maxIterations:)","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"metadata":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"stressMajorizationLayout"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"initial"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:12GraphDrawing0B0V","text":"Drawing"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":">?, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"edgeLength"},{"kind":"text","text":": ("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa","text":"Edges"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa","text":"Index"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd","text":"Double"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"tolerance"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd","text":"Double"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"maxIterations"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:12GraphDrawing0B0V","text":"Drawing"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"remoteSource":{"fileName":"StressMajorizationLayout.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/GraphDrawing\/StressMajorizationLayout.swift#L39"},"title":"stressMajorizationLayout(initial:edgeLength:tolerance:maxIterations:)","role":"symbol","modules":[{"name":"GraphDrawing","relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"]}],"externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P0A7DrawingE24stressMajorizationLayout7initial10edgeLength9tolerance13maxIterationsAD0C0Vy6VertexQzGANSg_Sd5Edges_5IndexQZXESdSitF","roleHeading":"Instance Method","extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","symbolKind":"method"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/graphdrawing\/graphprotocols\/graph\/stressmajorizationlayout(initial:edgelength:tolerance:maxiterations:)"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing","doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"]]},"kind":"sym